+## Deliberate limits and next work
 
-The 24,528-line domain unit and 4,466-line legacy replay-ledger unit remain
-review/build bottlenecks. Durable crash ordering also still needs a
-fault-injecting VFS and executable state oracle.
+The project has strong authenticity, replay, generation, transaction, and
+restart-evidence machinery, but no explicit end-to-end content-confidentiality
+or metadata-privacy model was found. Transport possession material is exposed
+as ordinary `std::string shared_secret` values. Before calling AnonSync private,
+define the adversary, key lifecycle, secret-memory policy, payload encryption,
+metadata leakage, revocation, and recovery model.
+
+“Convergence” is extensively implemented as manifests, lineage, conflict copies,
+receipts, workorders, and restart checkpoints, but there is no formal algebra or
+executable reference model proving strong eventual consistency. Do not market
+AnonSync as a CRDT until operations are classified, merge laws are stated, and
+reordering/duplication/partition traces are model-checked or property-tested.
+
+Crash correctness remains the highest-value systems gap. Add a fault-injecting
+VFS and an executable post-crash oracle that cuts every write/sync boundary,
+reorders or corrupts unsynchronized writes, restarts, and proves that each
+operation is wholly committed or reconstructibly absent. Exact VFS identity is
+not media durability.
+
+The main engineering bottleneck is still structural: `src/sync_domain.cpp` is
+24,530 lines; `src/reporting_selftests.cpp` 4,498;
+`src/sqlite_replay_ledger.cpp` 4,466; and the public header 3,499. Continue
+extracting libraries by invariant ownership, then migrate the explicit debt of
+40 raw opens, 70 raw transaction-control sites, 17 raw prepares, four legacy
+`sqlite3_close_v2` calls, three raw-pointer compatibility declarations, and one
+generic owner-borrow mint.
 
